The port's own source code is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 —
see the LICENSE file. This NOTICE file is part of that distribution and must be
redistributed with it, as Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires.

It is a reimplementation in Rust of the algorithms in OctoMap C++ 1.10.0
(commit f012f5f0a4f58cad19501833f9c0ea9d864427b6), written to reproduce that
library's observable behavior. No OctoMap source code is vendored or compiled
into this project, and there is no link-time dependency on it. The C++ sources
are used only as a reference during development and to generate the test
fixtures under tests/golden/.

Because the port reproduces the original work's behavior rather than being an
independent implementation from published papers, the original work's BSD
3-Clause terms are retained and reproduced in full below, as clauses 1 and 2
require. Those terms continue to govern the original OctoMap work regardless of
the license applied to this port.

